                            {
                                "target_word": "commit",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8947aa88-c1f4-3298-94fa-effb67d580b0",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To give in trust; to put into charge or keeping; to entrust; to consign; used with to or formerly unto."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a944b721-9e5a-4691-97a4-e0f9e7011350",
                                                "sense_id": "8947aa88-c1f4-3298-94fa-effb67d580b0",
                                                "text": "Bid him farwell, commit him to the Graue,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e62c91f2-382a-49b0-9ed2-2630656fb72e",
                                                "sense_id": "8947aa88-c1f4-3298-94fa-effb67d580b0",
                                                "text": "Commit thy way vnto the Lord: trust also in him, and he shall bring it to passe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e099c537-d243-44e8-b5d7-c435987ad81b",
                                                "sense_id": "8947aa88-c1f4-3298-94fa-effb67d580b0",
                                                "text": "If we take in hand any Volume; of Divinity or School Metaphyſics, for Inſtance; let us aſk, Does it contain any abſtract Reaſonings concerning Quantity or Number? No. Does it contain any experimental Reaſonings concerning Matters of Fact or Exiſtence? No. Commit it then to the Flames: For it can contain nothing but Sophiſtry and Illuſion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5682ad53-73f0-3864-b9d8-26b68da7fb5a",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To imprison: to forcibly place in a jail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0da999cc-1959-43df-9ba6-249969860469",
                                                "sense_id": "5682ad53-73f0-3864-b9d8-26b68da7fb5a",
                                                "text": "and ſome of the Conſpirators committed to the Caſtle of Dublin by us"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09a5bb42-101d-31c9-93bd-446541a3e01a",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To forcibly evaluate and treat in a medical facility, particularly for presumed mental illness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0baa59e7-5489-4cfe-8e20-5e63b9a703d4",
                                                "sense_id": "09a5bb42-101d-31c9-93bd-446541a3e01a",
                                                "text": "Tony should be committed to a nuthouse!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a5a48b1-fcee-3cf8-9048-cc6c8d488588",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To do (something bad); to perpetrate, as a crime, sin, or fault."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "033757aa-fc59-409f-9cb6-edd8a100ba08",
                                                "sense_id": "9a5a48b1-fcee-3cf8-9048-cc6c8d488588",
                                                "text": "to commit murder"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c20b27af-f6a8-467e-a465-e55b7319946c",
                                                "sense_id": "9a5a48b1-fcee-3cf8-9048-cc6c8d488588",
                                                "text": "to commit a series of heinous crimes"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c949a4cb-b991-473d-9196-0de89ce1495b",
                                                "sense_id": "9a5a48b1-fcee-3cf8-9048-cc6c8d488588",
                                                "text": "to commit suicide",
                                                "translation": "(also see usage notes)",
                                                "english": "(also see usage notes)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "681bc24a-44f5-40dc-91ff-7f1c3ff3ec1b",
                                                "sense_id": "9a5a48b1-fcee-3cf8-9048-cc6c8d488588",
                                                "text": "Thou shalt not commit adultery."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb409cdc-19ab-31eb-a34d-541908ba97d9",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pledge or bind; to compromise, expose, or endanger by some decisive act or preliminary step. (Traditionally used only reflexively but now also without oneself etc.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4f93684-4b01-44a0-a963-393156a120cd",
                                                "sense_id": "eb409cdc-19ab-31eb-a34d-541908ba97d9",
                                                "text": "to commit oneself to a certain action"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ec2bf9a-47ce-411d-ab69-6e2dbe8818df",
                                                "sense_id": "eb409cdc-19ab-31eb-a34d-541908ba97d9",
                                                "text": "to commit to a relationship"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "553a929d-18fe-46af-988f-7796906235aa",
                                                "sense_id": "eb409cdc-19ab-31eb-a34d-541908ba97d9",
                                                "text": "8 March, 1769, Junius, letter to the Duke of Grafton\nYou might have satisfied every duty of political friendship, without committing the honour of your sovereign."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e26d6e2d-e915-49a8-9557-9d48ca7c8dc2",
                                                "sense_id": "eb409cdc-19ab-31eb-a34d-541908ba97d9",
                                                "text": "Any sudden assent to the proposal[…]might possibly be considered as committing the faith of the United States."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0659def-be91-43d8-9782-c65e0592d2fd",
                                                "sense_id": "eb409cdc-19ab-31eb-a34d-541908ba97d9",
                                                "text": "[…] the perennial bachelor and “the single woman who has never married, who is afraid to commit to an apartment, because she's afraid if she somehow commits to a studio or one-bedroom then she's never going to get married,” said Julie Friedman, a senior associate broker at Bellmarc Realty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e22155b-1721-4ee6-bf57-1d565c6eb43b",
                                                "sense_id": "eb409cdc-19ab-31eb-a34d-541908ba97d9",
                                                "text": "And what actinic, mind-wrenching form could the countermeme take? How could human hands assemble something so devastatingly powerful and hold it steady; what human mind could wield it without exploding from the inside out? What would deploying that concept in anger do to human ideatic space? How far out from the solution is modern memetic science, a year, a century? What insane impossibility has Hughes just committed himself to?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "302dbf18-babc-357a-b169-972bdd499429",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a set of changes permanent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85b50bb5-5d57-4ebc-b592-68d89f047544",
                                                "sense_id": "302dbf18-babc-357a-b169-972bdd499429",
                                                "text": "When all SQL statements in the transaction are executed successfully, the transaction is committed and all the work that the SQL statements performed is made a permanent part of the database."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "059a27e4-b80c-4ef6-b7fd-a46ba2c25bdd",
                                                "sense_id": "302dbf18-babc-357a-b169-972bdd499429",
                                                "text": "We can commit all unstaged files with one command: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6be70b7-3447-3cdd-bfc3-9a559032f179",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To integrate new revisions into the public or master version of a file in a version control system."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00a63a9d-15cd-36d6-a6d7-50fff4435068",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To enter into a contest; to match; often followed by with."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6601c47e-6e5c-42b3-87c5-c07e7867fa85",
                                                "sense_id": "00a63a9d-15cd-36d6-a6d7-50fff4435068",
                                                "text": "For, in theſe ſtrifes, and on ſuch perſons, were as wretched to affect a victorie, as it is vnhappy to be committed with them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76252ab6-eded-4540-b0ea-3fd139f0f1ac",
                                                "sense_id": "00a63a9d-15cd-36d6-a6d7-50fff4435068",
                                                "text": "[…]and from hence ( as when Fire and Water are committed together ) ariſeth a most troubleſome conflict."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02d784e1-7afa-4bcf-a8e4-e31444a1fb71",
                                                "sense_id": "00a63a9d-15cd-36d6-a6d7-50fff4435068",
                                                "text": "[…]whilst it commits us in hostility with the three greatest military powers of the empire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db5d3bc9-2bad-34fd-89b6-5e253c02a8cc",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To confound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Latinism",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29ca73e8-f629-4289-af92-6c1a40382d58",
                                                "sense_id": "db5d3bc9-2bad-34fd-89b6-5e253c02a8cc",
                                                "text": "Harry whoſe tuneful and well meaſur'd Song / Firſt taught our Engliſh Muſick how to ſpan / Words with juſt note and accent, not to ſcan / With Midas Ears, committing ſhort and long;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2cd3a15-9790-3de6-b14b-00fc691b02ed",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To commit an offence; especially, to fornicate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33f4e940-2c10-4435-b0a7-2a23dc97c20e",
                                                "sense_id": "f2cd3a15-9790-3de6-b14b-00fc691b02ed",
                                                "text": "the sonne might one day bee found committing with his mother[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b310ef5-7285-429c-8067-a26fe3fea8c6",
                                                "sense_id": "f2cd3a15-9790-3de6-b14b-00fc691b02ed",
                                                "text": "[K]eepe thy words Iusſtice, ſweare not, commit not, with mans ſworne Spouſe;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "375cef2c-b4fa-3f60-ada2-b150e52f92b4",
                                        "entry_id": "90c79094-60a7-3163-9e8e-8604d12d60f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be committed or perpetrated; to take place; to occur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98a1279e-298a-4ff1-b253-374783dfe678",
                                                "sense_id": "375cef2c-b4fa-3f60-ada2-b150e52f92b4",
                                                "text": "As a vaſt Herd of Cows in a rich Farmer's Yard, if, while they are milked, they hear their Calves at a Diſtance, lamenting the Robbery which is then committing, roar and bellow: So roared forth the Somerſetſhire Mob an Hallaloo, made up of almoſt as many Squawls, Screams, and other different Sounds, as there were Perſons, or indeed Paſſions, among them: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
